# What this repository keeps, and what it does not.
#
# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist: everything at the root is excluded and the parts
# worth versioning are named back in. A denylist here would be wrong — the
# working directory accumulates scans, crops, checkpoints and rendered pages
# faster than anyone can remember to exclude them, and the failure mode is
# silent: a 400 dpi column PNG committed once is in the history forever.
#
# John's rule, 2026-08-09: anything we can download again (the scan PDF) or
# generate again (review pages, crops, kraken checkpoints) stays out. The
# pipeline, the reader outputs and the corpus stay in.
#
# ⚠ AN ALLOWLIST FAILS SILENTLY IN THE OTHER DIRECTION TOO. The first version of
# this file kept out `pyproject.toml` — without which the package will not even
# install — along with five of the six readers' outputs, the persisted
# adversarial reviews, and the explainer. Nothing complained; they were simply
# not there. When adding a directory, check `git status --short --ignored`
# rather than assuming the rules below still cover it.

/*
!.gitignore
!*.md

# The package itself, and the resolved dependency set the tests ran against.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!bonitz_pipeline/
!tests/
!run_pilot_compare.py

# The explainer and anything else written to be read by a person.
!docs/

# EVERY reader's output, not just the adjudicator's. The whole method here is
# that independent readers disagree and the disagreement is the signal, so
# keeping only `opus` would throw away the evidence and leave the verdicts
# unfalsifiable.
!raw/

!work/
work/*
!work/reconciled/
!work/adjudicated/
!work/verdicts/
!work/damage/
!work/segmenter-gaps/
!work/corrigenda/
!work/sigla/
!work/rulings/
!work/sweeps/
!work/lexcheck/
!work/recheck/
!work/prompts/
!work/flags-by-col/
!work/flags4-by-col/
!work/flags5-by-col/
!work/aristotle-forms.json

# ⚠ THE EXPORT SPLIT AND ITS PAIRING, BECAUSE LOSING THEM COST A REAL THING.
# On 2026-08-20 the kraken400 arrow was recompiled and the out-of-fold read
# died with it: `train-oof.tsv` is indexed positionally against an export
# ordering that existed only inside that arrow, and the fold maps address the
# same vanished positions. Nothing under work/kraken400 had ever been in git,
# so there was no earlier state to recover it from.
#
# The arrows stay ignored — 200 MB, and recompilable. What is versioned is the
# SPLIT and the SEGMENTATION: seg/*.xml never changes, work/reconciled is
# already tracked, and `kraken_corpus pair` is deterministic over the two. So
# any past commit can regenerate its own gt/ and its own export ordering, and
# an index like the OOF's stops being a thing that can only be lost.
#
# holdout.txt is the one that must never drift unnoticed: it is which columns
# John held out, and a model's honesty rests on it.
!work/kraken400/
work/kraken400/*
!work/kraken400/seg/
!work/kraken400/train.txt
!work/kraken400/holdout.txt
!work/kraken400/pairing.json
!work/kraken-cold/
work/kraken-cold/*
!work/kraken-cold/seg/
!work/kraken-cold/train.txt
!work/kraken-cold/holdout.txt
!work/kraken-cold/pairing.json
# The ground-truth audit: candidate queues and JOHN'S RULINGS. The crops and
# the built page are regenerable from the corpus and stay ignored; the
# rulings are not regenerable from anything and must never live only in an
# ignored path (an allowlist fails silently — check with
# `git status --short --ignored` after editing this block).
!work/audit/
work/audit/crops/
work/audit/*.html
work/audit/server.log

# The adversarial reviews, persisted deliberately: two finished ones were lost
# to a reboot on 2026-08-09 because they lived only in a temp directory, and a
# review nobody read is indistinguishable from a review nobody ran.
!work/reviews/

!work/kraken/
# ⚠ THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST AND IT FAILS IN SILENCE. Everything under work/ is
# ignored unless named here, so a new output directory is simply absent from
# `git status` and looks like work that was never done. It has cost this repo
# five of six reader outputs for a day. After writing any new artifact under
# work/, run `git status --short --ignored` and check it is not on the !! list.
!work/reconciled-auto/
!work/reconciled-auto-checks/
!work/queue-053-062.json
!work/queue-review-53-62.json
!work/queue-review-15-102.json
!work/queue-followup-2026-08-18.json
!work/flags5-gt-015-052.jsonl
!work/flags5-gt-by-col/
!work/settle-gt-report.txt
work/kraken/*
!work/kraken/
# ⚠ THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST AND IT FAILS IN SILENCE. Everything under work/ is
# ignored unless named here, so a new output directory is simply absent from
# `git status` and looks like work that was never done. It has cost this repo
# five of six reader outputs for a day. After writing any new artifact under
# work/, run `git status --short --ignored` and check it is not on the !! list.
!work/reconciled-auto/
!work/reconciled-auto-checks/
!work/queue-053-062.json
!work/flags5-gt-015-052.jsonl
!work/flags5-gt-by-col/
!work/settle-gt-report.txt
!NOTES.md

# Review pages are build artifacts and they are not small — book-review.html is
# 6.7 MB of base64 crops on its own. Every one regenerates from its module:
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.mark_review    --html <path>
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.book_review
#   python3 -m bonitz_pipeline.siglum_review
work/sweeps/*.html

# The five-model calamari ensemble: its EVIDENCE, never its models. 71 MB of
# SavedModels lives in ~/Developer/bonitz-models/ and is reproducible; the
# evaluation log, the fold configs and the digests are neither, and a claim of
# 0.82% CER with nothing behind it is not a claim.
!work/calamari/
work/calamari/*
!work/calamari/*.tsv
!work/calamari/ensemble5/
# calamari's out-of-fold read of the training set: the predictions and the
# fold maps, which are the evidence the out-of-fold claim can be checked
# against. The 4,693 raw per-line files and the runner log live beside the
# models in ~/Developer/bonitz-models/oof-2026-08-14/.
!work/calamari/oof/
!work/calamari/oof-vs-corpus.tsv

# The one holdout both engines were scored on, and the three files a reader
# needs to recompute 0.3303% and 0.4582% without a GPU. The 11 MB of ALTO
# under eval-e11/ stays out — the text is the evidence, the glyph coordinates
# are not. [[an-authority-claims-more-than-its-evidence]]
#   holdout.txt        the 12 columns, in the order everything scores them
#   holdout-gt.tsv     the ground truth AS TRAINED — see kraken_corpus's
#                      BEKKER_SPACE; it is NOT work/reconciled/
#   e11-holdout-pred.tsv   kraken round 6, epoch 11
!work/kraken15-102/
work/kraken15-102/*
!work/kraken15-102/holdout.txt
!work/kraken15-102/holdout-gt.tsv
!work/kraken15-102/e11-holdout-pred.tsv

# The queues the 107-117 apply actually ran through. Two of them are BUILT —
# `site_queue` re-anchors John's ink readings and the homoglyph sweep onto the
# current spine — so without them there is no record of which offsets his 257
# rulings were applied at, and the run cannot be repeated or checked.
!work/kraken15-102/apply/
!work/kraken15-102/apply/*.json

# The rulings themselves are the point, and they are tiny. Keep them.
!work/sweeps/*.json
!work/sweeps/*.tsv
!work/sweeps/*.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Ink crops cut for a review page. `!work/sweeps/` re-includes that directory
# and NOTHING below it was ignoring these — `ligature_review` says in a comment
# that `work/sweeps/crops/` is "already gitignored" and it never was, so 192
# PNGs of an 1870 scan have been sitting untracked-but-addable, with a bundled
# sitting about to add 471 more. `git add -f` has put three leaves of this book
# in a public repo once already (tests/test_no_scans_in_git.py). Every crop
# regenerates from its module.
work/sweeps/crops/
# ⚠ AND EVERY SIBLING. The literal path above ignored exactly one directory,
# and each new sitting cuts its own — `crops-cold5`, `crops-alphacheck-15-62`,
# `crops-qc-63-102` were all untracked-but-addable the moment they appeared.
# A named path is not a rule; the glob is.
work/sweeps/crops-*/
work/sweeps/*/crops/

# genie_split output — regenerable from raw/genie400/*.docx in one command,
# and 10MB. The ARCHIVES are the original and are tracked; this is not.
raw/genie-pages/
work/paddle-export/
work/paddle-dataset/
work/tesstrain/
